+# Ticket #4471: why new-UI users have no session replays
+
+## Cause
+
+Replay is built from screenshots taken by `PostHogWidget`. The legacy shell
+(`lib/legacy_app.dart`) wraps its `MaterialApp` in `PostHogWidget`. The new
+shell (`lib/new_app.dart`) builds `MaterialApp.router` without it. So the new
+UI sends events (screens, taps, `loan_amount_changed`, `application_submitted`)
+but no frames, and the Replay tab only has sessions from the old UI.
+
+Evidence:
+- `posthog_flutter` 5.55.0 source (`lib/src/posthog_widget.dart`): the widget's
+  state creates the `ScreenshotCapturer` and `NativeCommunicator` that feed
+  replay. Nothing else in the package produces replay frames on mobile.
+- Ticket: project settings are fine (recording on, sampling 100%, minimum
+  duration 0) and both groups use the same SDK version and build. The only
+  code difference between the groups is the wrapper.
+- `main.dart` calls `Analytics.init()` (which calls `Posthog().setup`) before
+  `runApp`, so the widget finds a config and starts capturing. Setup order is
+  not the cause.
+
+## Fix
+
+`lib/new_app.dart`: wrapped `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget` and added a
+comment saying why it must stay. `dart format` also reflowed the `theme:`
+block onto one line.
+
+No other files changed.
+
+## Which parts of the colleague's note applied
+
+Applied:
+- The core diagnosis: a `MaterialApp` without `PostHogWidget` records events
+  but no replay, with no error. This is the bug here.
+- The "check each `MaterialApp`" step: there are two shells, and only one had
+  the wrapper. This is the same mistake the note describes.
+- Step 1 and 2 of the checklist: `posthog_flutter: ^5.36.0` is in
+  `pubspec.yaml` (>= 5.14.0), and `sessionReplay = true` is set in
+  `lib/analytics.dart`.
+- Step 4: `PosthogObserver()` is in both shells (`navigatorObservers` in
+  legacy, `GoRouter.observers` in new), so screen splitting is already in
+  place.
+
+Not applicable, or already satisfied:
+- Step 3, `startSessionRecording()` behind a flag: not used here. Recording is
+  turned on by `config.sessionReplay = true` before setup, which is the
+  documented path.
+- Step 5, `maskAllTexts`: already set to `true` in `analytics.dart`.
+- Web / posthog-js notes: this is a mobile build, not relevant.
+- Sampling, retention, and project-setting checks: the ticket already rules
+  these out.
+
+## Not verified
+
+- I did not run the app on a device or emulator, so the fix is not confirmed
+  end to end. Verify with the steps in the colleague's note: run
+  `flutter run --dart-define=NEW_UI=true` on a device, go through 3-4 screens,
+  background the app, and check that the session appears in the Replay tab
+  with screenshots.
+- `flutter analyze lib/new_app.dart` passes with no issues.
+- Nothing was committed or deployed. The change needs a new release to reach
+  users.
